+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry is the validation boundary between model-produced JSON and consumer-written tool executors.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates input against the resolved tool definition before invoking its executor. Missing required properties, wrong types, and enum mismatches return a `ToolResponse` that names the failing property path and constraint without including the rejected value; no rejected input reaches the executor or appears in a log line. ([validated by: rejects missing and wrong-typed input without executing or disclosing values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L30)) Unknown tool names remain errors. ([validated by: uses each function-valued definition current at that call and keeps unknown-name errors](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L110))
+
+A static definition's schema is compiled when the tool is registered, so an invalid schema fails registration with the tool name and a valid schema is not recompiled for later executions. ([validated by: compiles schemas at the correct lifecycle and preserves accepted input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L68)) A function-valued definition is resolved and validated using the schema current for each call, with compilation cached only for that resolved schema object. ([validated by: uses each function-valued definition current at that call and keeps unknown-name errors](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L110))
+
+Validation neither adds an `additionalProperties: false` constraint nor coerces or defaults data. Accepted input, including unlisted properties, reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once. ([validated by: compiles schemas at the correct lifecycle and preserves accepted input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L68))
